.TH TENSOR_UTILS 1 "2026-06-29" "Symoneural" "Symoneural Helper Utilities"
.SH NAME
tensor_utils \- safetensors and GGUF tensor inspection, slicing, and dtype casting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python helpers/python/tensor_utils.py
.I path
.RB [ \-\-tensor
.IR NAME ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tensor_utils.py
is a command-line tool and importable Python module for inspecting
.I .safetensors
files.  It lists tensor names, shapes, dtypes, and memory sizes, and
optionally filters output to a single named tensor.
.PP
The module also provides helpers for casting tensors between dtypes
and for estimating GGUF quantised block sizes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I path
Path to the
.B .safetensors
file to inspect.
.TP
.B \-\-tensor \fINAME\fR
Print information for only the tensor named
.IR NAME .
If omitted, all tensors are listed.
.SH OUTPUT
JSON array of tensor descriptors.  Each entry has the fields:
.RS
.IP name
Tensor key name inside the file.
.IP shape
List of dimension sizes.
.IP dtype
NumPy dtype string (e.g.
.BR float32 ).
.IP nbytes
Memory footprint in bytes.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
List all tensors:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/tensor_utils.py model.safetensors
.EE
.RE
.PP
Show one tensor:
.RS
.EX
python helpers/python/tensor_utils.py model.safetensors \-\-tensor model.embed_tokens.weight
.EE
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHONPATH
Must include
.B helpers/python/
if running from a directory other than the repo root.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B safetensors
(pip install safetensors),
.B numpy
(pip install numpy).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gguf_inspect (1),
.BR lora_merge (1),
.BR quant_utils (1)
.SH AUTHORS
Symoneural contributors.
